e/conf#transfer","content":"| Field     | Default | Meaning                                                                                                                              |\n| --------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `enabled` | `false` | Enable Transfer routing in this process. On a client, `load` and `export` use Transfer; on a Transfer server, it starts the service. |","locale":"en","table":"table-11"},"1253":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf-335","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf#transfer","content":"| Field       | Default                                                 | Meaning                                                                                                                                                                |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `store_url` | empty; inferred as `sqlite://data/transfer/transfer.db` | State store URL. Schemes: `memory://`, `sqlite://`, `mysql://`, `postgres://`, `postgresql://`. Use one shared `mysql://` or `postgres://` URL for multiple instances. |","locale":"en","table":"table-11"},"1254":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf-336","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf#transfer","content":"| Field      | Default     | Meaning                                                            |\n| ---------- | ----------- | --------------------------------------------------