rvine adopts a layered distributed architecture design that ensures clear component responsibilities with excellent scalability and high availability. The entire architecture is primarily divided into three layers: **control layer** (Master), **storage layer** (Workers), and **access layer** (clients: FUSE, SDK, CLI), which collaborate to complete data storage, processing, and management tasks.","locale":"en"},"1859":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-5","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"Curvine consists of three main server-side roles plus clients and UFS:","locale":"en"},"1860":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-6","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**Curvine Client**: Data read/write operations are implemented by the client, which calls Curvine server-side interfaces through RPC (metadata from Master, block data from Workers). The client supports multiple access methods:","locale":"en"},"1861":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-7","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**FUSE Mount**: POSIX-compatible mount via libfuse/3 (curvine-fuse)","locale":"en"},"1862":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-8","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**HDFS & SDK**: Java / Python / libsdk interfaces","locale":"en"},"1863":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-9","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**CSI Driver**: Kubernetes volume driver (curvine-csi)","locale":"en"},"1864":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-10","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**CLI (`cv`)**: Admin tools for fs ops, report, and cluster management","locale":"en"},"1865":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-11","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"Internally, the client layer is composed of:","locale":"en"},"1866":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-12","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**UnifiedFileSystem**: Provides unified namespace with CurvineFS + UFS fallback","locale":"en"},"1867":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-13","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**FsReader / FsWriter**: Parallel, buffered I/O with zero-copy optimization","locale":"en"},"1868":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-14","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**BlockClient Pool**: Manages block_reader / block_writer for local and remote access","locale":"en"},"1869":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-15","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**Mount & Meta Cache**: Caches mount info and inode metadata","locale":"en"},"1870":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-16","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**Master**: The core control node; responsible for metadata (directory tree, file inodes, block locations), Worker registration, block allocation, and UFS mount table. Master can run as multiple nodes forming a Raft group for high availability; only the Raft leader serves metadata writes.","locale":"en"},"1871":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-17","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"The Master cluster mainly includes:","locale":"en"},"1872":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-18","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**MasterServer**: RPC handling and routing","locale":"en"},"1873":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-19","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**MasterFilesystem**: File system operations (mkdir, create, rename, delete, list)","locale":"en"},"1874":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-20","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**FsDir + InodeStore**: In-memory inode tree and metadata management","locale":"en"},"1875":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-21","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**JournalSystem**: Edit log and snapshot for recovery","locale":"en"},"1876":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-22","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**Worker / Mount Manager**: Worker heartbeat and UFS mount management","locale":"en"},"1877":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-23","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**Quota / Job / Replication**: Quota control, TTL, eviction, replication scheduling","locale":"en"},"1878":{"id":"/docs/Overview/architecture-24","page_id":"/docs/Overview/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Overview/architecture#architecture-overview","content":"**RocksDB Metadata Store**: Persistent metadata storage","locale":"en"},"1879":{"id":"/d