dard file operations, including random writes, concurrent writes, file locks, extended attributes, symbolic and hard links, sparse files, and preallocation. Existing local applications can migrate directly. |"],[2507,"| Core Capability              | Plain Explanation                                                                                                                       |\n| ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Intelligent space management | Uses TTL expiration and quota plus LRU eviction to manage storage space, preventing cache from occupying cluster capacity indefinitely. |"],[2506,"| Core Capability            | Plain Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| -------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Intelligent tiered storage | Supports multiple storage tiers such as memory (MEM), SSD, and HDD. Administrators configure paths for each tier in advance, and users can specify the preferred write medium. When the preferred tier lacks space, data automatically spills over to the next tier. |"],[2504,"| Core Capability   | Plain Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| ----------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Unified namespace | A single mount point can access all file directories. Users do not need to care which Worker node or storage medium stores the data. File paths and permissions are consistent with the local filesystem. |"],[760,"| Crate / Directory                                 | Role                  |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | --------------------- |\n| `curvine-master`, `curvine-worker`, `curvine-mds` | Service entry crates. |"],[758,"| Crate / Directory                     | Role                                         |\n| ------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `crates/server/curvine-data-transfer` | Standalone Load and Export Transfer service. |"],[762,"| Crate / Directory               | Role                                             |\n| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `crates/sdk/`, `curvine-libsdk` | Rust, Java, and Python SDK crates and packaging. |"],[756,"| Crate / Directory              | Role                                   |\n| ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------- |\n| `crates/metadata/curvine-raft` | Raft journal and metadata replication. |"],[757,"| Crate / Directory  | Role                                                                                                 |\n| ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `crates/adapters/` | RocksDB, local and SPDK storage, OpenDAL and OSS-HDFS UFS backends, HDFS JNI, and service discovery. |"],[754,"| Crate / Directory | Role                                                                            |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `crates/core/`    | Runtime, RPC, networking, I