e lower the latency. The larger the batch, the higher the throughput. In addition, because the Raft log already guarantees data consistency, RocksDB's own WAL log is disabled, further improving write speed."],[2560,"Automatic caching and proactive caching are not mutually exclusive. Proactive caching can reduce the time required for the first read of a UFS file."],[2555,"Automatic caching is enabled for a mount when that mount has a non-zero TTL, for example `cv mount s3://bucket/prefix /path --ttl-ms 7d`. On the first read of a UFS file under that mount, Curvine submits an asynchronous load job to bring the data into Curvine. The read is served from UFS while the job runs in the background. The job follows the same Transfer routing as a manual `cv load` command."],[3260,"Automatic caching is enabled per-mount when TTL > 0. First reads trigger background load jobs."],[6622,"Automatic caching is enabled per-mount when TTL > 0. First reads trigger background load jobs."],[3134,"Available Capacity: Currently available storage space of the node"],[1490,"Available Dockerfiles under `curvine-docker/compile/`:"],[3227,"Avoid kernels below 4.15 in production — FUSE concurrency is severely limited."],[6589,"Avoid kernels below 4.15 in production — FUSE concurrency is severely limited."],[831,"Avoid repeating unpublished storage or protocol promises that are not backed by the reference repository state."],[2108,"AWS CLI"],[5472,"AWS CLI"],[906,"Bare Metal Deployment"],[916,"Bare metal deployment requires manually starting the **cluster core** (master and worker). Optionally start FUSE on nodes where you need a POSIX mount:"],[541,"Based on the above environment and parameters, this test executed four metadata operations: `createWrite` (create write), `openRead` (open read), `rename` (rename), and `delete` (delete). Each operation was repeated 3 times, and the average value was taken as the final result to ensure the accuracy of the test data."],[1530,"Based on this reference,